  "policy": {
    "consistency": "Every shared resource byte position in a single multipart response must have identical values across all parts. Compare each new part against all previous parts; reject the whole response on a conflict.",
    "compatibility": "Identical duplicates, nesting, partial overlaps, reordered and nonadjacent overlaps remain allowed. Disjoint or adjacent parts need not have equal content. Existing request-bound and total-length checks still apply.",
    "representation": "Comparison is over octets after HTTP dechunking. Existing policy permits only absent/identity Content-Encoding and absent/binary Content-Transfer-Encoding. Parts are not decoded, rewritten or combined.",
    "bounds": "At most 16 parts gives 120 part pairs. For total part-content size S, overlap lengths sum to at most 15*S/2. The existing 10 MiB response budget bounds S; views avoid per-overlap copying or allocation by resource offset.",
    "numeric": "Relative offsets remain bounded by the actual part content, even near the local signed 63-bit resource-position ceiling. No first-position-sized buffer is allocated.",
    "delivery": "MCP buffers the bounded complete response and rejects a final read/validation error before returning content. Direct Go streaming users must read to EOF and honor the error.",
    "accounting": "Python shared cases verify consumed bytes are charged even on rejection; Go MCP retains its existing read-byte accounting before the read-error branch."
  },
